    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Boil the spaghetti in salted water until just shy of al dente, then drain, saving a cup of pasta water.",
                    "Meanwhile, brown the ground beef in your largest pot over medium-high heat, breaking it up and seasoning with the black pepper, until no pink remains; ground beef should hit 160F. Drain excess fat.",
                    "Add the garlic and cook 2 to 3 minutes, then stir in the taco seasoning and tomato paste.",
                    "Pour in the diced tomatoes and the diced tomatoes and green chilies with their juice and simmer 8 to 10 minutes until the sauce thickens.",
                    "Fold in the spaghetti with a splash of the reserved pasta water, then stir in the Mexican cheese blend until it melts into the sauce.",
                    "Top with the mozzarella, cover on low heat 3 to 4 minutes until melted, then finish with the sliced olives and chopped cilantro."
                ],
